<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-ALL AVERAGES ON INTERBANK LOAN RATES DECREASE.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-ALL AVERAGES ON INTERBANK LOAN RATES DECREASE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank loan rates</p>
<p>decreased over the last week, the central bank said on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;All banks are still very liquid and are waiting for better</p>
<p>investment opportunities,&quot; said Ege Metsandi from Hansapank's</p>
<p>interest rate product department.</p>
<p>The other reason cited for the decrease is in the Swap</p>
<p>calculation methods. The new method is based on DM interest</p>
<p>rates plus a marginal, instead of the previous local money</p>
<p>market interest rate used before, she added.</p>
<p> TALIBOR/TALBID    One Week    One Month    Three Months</p>
<p> April 02	   4.67/3.67    6.22/5.22    7.98/6.98</p>
<p> April 09	   4.50/3.50    6.08/5.08    7.52/6.52</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
<p>reuters@reuters.ee</p>
